131
00:09:19,440 --> 00:09:20,380
My name is Rhys Gray.

132
00:09:20,380 --> 00:09:23,560
I'm a Cardiac Imaging Fellow at Bart's Heart Centre in London.

133
00:09:27,240 --> 00:09:30,020
In this case, we have an 18-year-old male

134
00:09:30,020 --> 00:09:33,160
who presented to hospital with palpitations and dizziness.

135
00:09:34,440 --> 00:09:37,220
His ECG showed for wide complex tachycardia

136
00:09:37,220 --> 00:09:40,520
and he underwent successful DC cardioversion.

137
00:09:41,860 --> 00:09:43,360
He has no past medical history.

138
00:09:44,080 --> 00:09:45,780
He's on no regular medications,

139
00:09:45,780 --> 00:09:48,720
but he does have a family history of cardiomyopathy

140
00:09:48,720 --> 00:09:51,560
in his mother who had a permanent pacemaker

141
00:09:51,560 --> 00:09:54,900
implanted in her 40s for early conduction disease.

142
00:09:56,460 --> 00:10:00,380
Sinus ECG shows pre-excitation and conduction disease.

143
00:10:01,560 --> 00:10:04,900
Transthoracic echocardiogram and cardiac MRI were performed.

144
00:10:08,380 --> 00:10:12,140
This is the 12-lead ECG post-cardioversion.

145
00:10:15,780 --> 00:10:20,000
This is the transthoracic echocardiogram

146
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:24,440
with the parasternal long-axis cine on the left

147
00:10:24,440 --> 00:10:27,620
and the four-chamber on the far right.

148
00:10:33,620 --> 00:10:36,260
These are the cardiac MRI images.

149
00:10:36,920 --> 00:10:40,560
On the far left, this is the short-axis cine stack

150
00:10:40,560 --> 00:10:42,720
showing the wall thickness.

151
00:10:42,720 --> 00:10:46,400
In the middle is the late gadolinium,

152
00:10:47,080 --> 00:10:48,180
late contrast images.

153
00:10:51,460 --> 00:10:54,980
And on the far right is the T1 map.

154
00:11:04,140 --> 00:11:06,040
What is the most likely diagnosis?

155
00:11:06,580 --> 00:11:08,460
Okay, so he's asked you a question.

156
00:11:08,580 --> 00:11:10,000
What is the most likely diagnosis?

157
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:12,500
Is it A-A-T-T-R amyloid?

158
00:11:12,900 --> 00:11:15,000
Is it titan cardiomyopathy,

159
00:11:15,460 --> 00:11:16,940
hypertrophic cardiomyopathy,

160
00:11:17,420 --> 00:11:18,440
Fabry's disease,

161
00:11:18,760 --> 00:11:20,000
or Danone disease?

162
00:11:21,520 --> 00:11:22,620
Please vote now.

163
00:11:23,960 --> 00:11:25,060
So, what do you think?

164
00:11:25,380 --> 00:11:25,840
Firstly,

165
00:11:26,400 --> 00:11:28,140
I think it's genetic, yes?

166
00:11:28,680 --> 00:11:29,640
Yes, the mum.

167
00:11:30,460 --> 00:11:31,880
What about the ECG?

168
00:11:31,880 --> 00:11:33,220
We've noticed something.

169
00:11:33,220 --> 00:11:34,800
It's kind of going off the scale, isn't it?

170
00:11:36,240 --> 00:11:36,760
Firstly,

171
00:11:37,220 --> 00:11:38,460
quite high voltage.

172
00:11:38,840 --> 00:11:39,140
Yes.

173
00:11:39,300 --> 00:11:40,780
Consistent with hypertrophy

174
00:11:40,780 --> 00:11:41,780
that we see over there.

175
00:11:42,180 --> 00:11:44,540
And this accessory pathway.

176
00:11:44,880 --> 00:11:45,140
Yeah.

177
00:11:45,680 --> 00:11:47,700
What about,

178
00:11:47,880 --> 00:11:51,140
you're an expert in MRIs.

179
00:11:51,300 --> 00:11:53,300
What do you think about the gadolinium pattern?

180
00:11:53,300 --> 00:11:56,240
So, we have quite a patchy distribution

181
00:11:56,240 --> 00:11:57,880
of the gadolinium,

182
00:11:58,180 --> 00:12:00,660
which usually indicates replacement fibrosis.

183
00:12:01,160 --> 00:12:02,960
And we can notice on the echo

184
00:12:02,960 --> 00:12:05,100
that there is the ventricle,

185
00:12:05,160 --> 00:12:05,900
as well as the cardiomyopathy,

186
00:12:05,980 --> 00:12:07,060
the ventricle is quite thickened

187
00:12:07,060 --> 00:12:09,240
with good radial contractility,

188
00:12:09,380 --> 00:12:11,640
but reduced longitudinal.

189
00:12:12,400 --> 00:12:13,560
And, okay,

190
00:12:13,680 --> 00:12:14,860
the boat has now closed.

191
00:12:16,460 --> 00:12:17,020
Okay.

192
00:12:18,680 --> 00:12:19,800
Let's have a look at the answer.

193
00:12:19,800 --> 00:12:22,980
The correct answer is E,

194
00:12:23,480 --> 00:12:24,200
Danone disease.

195
00:12:25,260 --> 00:12:26,500
Let's have a look why.

196
00:12:29,580 --> 00:12:30,260
Okay.

197
00:12:30,400 --> 00:12:33,140
So, you've seen that very abnormal ECG,

198
00:12:33,560 --> 00:12:35,340
which Philip pointed out.

199
00:12:35,820 --> 00:12:37,260
There's pre-excitation,

200
00:12:37,820 --> 00:12:38,880
conduction disease.

201
00:12:39,540 --> 00:12:41,400
It's not a normal ECG.

202
00:12:42,520 --> 00:12:44,260
You've got LVH,

203
00:12:44,460 --> 00:12:46,080
probably by voltage criteria,

204
00:12:46,080 --> 00:12:47,120
if you believe that.

205
00:12:47,400 --> 00:12:49,020
There's also LV dysfunction,

206
00:12:49,020 --> 00:12:50,820
hypertrophy on the imaging,

207
00:12:51,240 --> 00:12:52,180
and a very abnormal

208
00:12:52,180 --> 00:12:53,360
late enhancement pattern.

209
00:12:54,200 --> 00:12:54,860
And a young man

210
00:12:54,860 --> 00:12:57,040
with very severe phenotype,

211
00:12:57,120 --> 00:12:58,560
which is more severe than his mother,

212
00:12:59,040 --> 00:13:01,240
it makes Danone the most likely diagnosis,

213
00:13:01,440 --> 00:13:02,580
which is X-linked.

214
00:13:02,940 --> 00:13:04,080
It's been confirmed,

215
00:13:04,180 --> 00:13:04,740
in this case,

216
00:13:04,820 --> 00:13:05,820
with genetic testing,

217
00:13:06,160 --> 00:13:07,580
and he had a LAMP2

218
00:13:07,580 --> 00:13:09,500
gene-positive abnormality.

219
00:13:09,500 --> 00:13:13,520
This is the first case report

220
00:13:13,520 --> 00:13:14,440
from the Middle East,

221
00:13:14,600 --> 00:13:16,400
from hospital in Sharjah,

222
00:13:16,920 --> 00:13:18,720
Mahmud Ramadan Al-Muafi,

223
00:13:18,800 --> 00:13:22,220
very grateful for this excellent set of images

224
00:13:22,220 --> 00:13:23,920
of a post-mortem heart

225
00:13:23,920 --> 00:13:26,160
prior to transplantation,

226
00:13:26,260 --> 00:13:29,460
showing that fibrosis that you see.

227
00:13:29,460 --> 00:13:30,400
So,

228
00:13:31,300 --> 00:13:33,180
atypical late enhancement for amyloid,

229
00:13:33,620 --> 00:13:35,360
Titan usually gives you a DCM pattern,

230
00:13:35,740 --> 00:13:37,740
there's no outflow tract obstruction,

231
00:13:38,680 --> 00:13:40,820
and Fabrice normally gives you a low T1

232
00:13:40,820 --> 00:13:43,300
with some infralateral fibrosis.

233
00:13:45,300 --> 00:13:47,600
So, let's see how you all did

234
00:13:47,600 --> 00:13:48,760
